  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $6:7$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{7}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of apples and the denominator represents the total number of fruits.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 5}{7\\times 5}=\\frac{30}{35}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Jason has $35$ fruits in total. So, the number of peaches Jason has is\n\n$$\n35-30=5.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
